# Text files end their lines with LF in every checkout, on every system, whatever a machine's
# core.autocrlf says. Tests read tracked files (the guards scan sources, scripts and docs): with
# autocrlf a file written on Windows had LF until git next touched it and CRLF in every fresh
# checkout, so a test could pass in the tree it was written in and fail everywhere else (M5's
# last push: crates/specula/tests/line_endings.rs holds this file in place).
* text=auto eol=lf
